# Review ownership for the release path.
#
# GitHub consults this file ONLY when it evaluates pull request reviews. On its own it blocks
# nothing. What enforces it is whichever org ruleset currently applies to THIS branch, and that
# differs by branch and changes over time:
#
#   test, prod  -- a pull request is required and these paths need a code owner's approval.
#   dev         -- locked to the org owner outright; there is no pull-request path, so this
#                  file is dormant here and becomes the gate the moment that lock is lifted.
#
# There are three branches and only three. `main` was deleted on the remote in all fourteen repos
# on 2026-08-21 and this header named it until then. The org ruleset `lock-main-and-dev` still
# lists `refs/heads/main` in its `include`, which is now inert -- narrowing it is a separate,
# deliberate edit, because that one rule covers `dev` as well.
#
# It is kept on dev deliberately, ahead of need: when the locks are reversed, the protection
# is already in place rather than being remembered afterwards.
#
# CODEOWNERS is read from the branch a pull request TARGETS, never from the default branch,
# which is why it exists on each branch separately. A copy missing from one branch protects
# nothing there and fails silently, by requesting no review at all.
#
# Ordinary changes need no approval -- the rule asks for zero. Only the paths below require one.

